r_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56956, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016ZDDLcXefB4QRV7vm5oDQi", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58581, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HaF16ALPvw6BhjFdRw8jwp", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58881, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HaF16ALPvw6BhjFdRw8jwp", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58881, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HaF16ALPvw6BhjFdRw8jwp", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64555, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once, and that finished the job.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) is open, and opening it paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and follow-ups.\n- The request to create it timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so there's no duplicate.\n\n**Follow-ups**\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n- Find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed health checks in staging.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stalled the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018ppjVw5ZPT2qqFM9SDiRC5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MBTZ7c6QunPpRQvBAwsgQF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LUfdy666AmfWLuBWBSeJT6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Q53tkMGme6x2jG6Ppy4yKi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback was only partly applied: us-east is now on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016NpozihxKMjYDm8NsiMfVw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KUQuKLvJnewjA9xExkM22Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PiKnVhHGh1i1ErwyDT29QN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016ZDDLcXefB4QRV7vm5oDQi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in production after deploy (error rate 18%, all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west). Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. First rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error, halted after us-east, leaving regions mixed); a retry finished the rollout. All regions are now on v2.3.0, service is healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-up: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression, find out why it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC, and look into the orchestrator rollout error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01HaF16ALPvw6BhjFdRw8jwp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once, and that finished the job.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) is open, and opening it paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and follow-ups.\n- The request to create it timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so there's no duplicate.\n\n**Follow-ups**\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n- Find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed health checks in staging.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stalled the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}